# --- Local sync (no setup needed) ---
# Syncing your real Google Sheet (npm run sync / the Admin panel's "Sync
# now" button) needs no credentials at all — it reads the sheet's public
# CSV export, which works as long as the sheet is shared as "Anyone with
# the link can view". See README.md for the security tradeoffs of this
# approach (it exposes the whole spreadsheet, not just the 4 synced tabs).
# Only needed if syncing a different sheet than the one already configured
# in config/data-sources.ts:
# GOOGLE_SHEETS_SPREADSHEET_ID=YOUR_TA_TRACKER_SPREADSHEET_ID

# --- Required only when you're ready for shared/production hosting ---
# Setting these switches auth from the local demo store to real Supabase
# Auth, and data storage from the local SQLite file to Supabase Postgres
# (Project Settings -> API).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxxxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
# Server-only — bypasses RLS. Never expose to the browser or commit it.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key

# --- Production sheet sync: pick ONE of the two options below ---

# Option A — Google Apps Script Web App (recommended — no Google Cloud
# Console project needed, sheet is never made public). See
# docs/google-apps-script-setup.md for the script to paste in and deploy.
# GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=https://script.google.com/macros/s/xxxxx/exec
# GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_SECRET=a-long-random-secret-you-generate

# Option B — authenticated Sheets API via a Google Cloud service account.
# Used automatically if GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL above isn't set. See
# README.md "Ready for real users / production hosting" for setup steps.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=ta-dashboard-sync@your-project.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# Paste the private_key from the service account JSON key, keeping \n escapes as-is.
# GOOGLE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# --- Qandle HRMS (Attrition tab) ---
# Credentials come from your HR team / Qandle contact (see "Qandle Api -
# guide"). Leave unset and the Attrition tab simply shows a "not
# connected" message — the Google Sheet sync is unaffected. The secret stays
# server-side: never commit it or put it in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
# QANDLE_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id
# QANDLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret
# Only if the base URL ever changes:
# QANDLE_BASE_URL=https://your-company.qandle.com

# HR exits sheet (the Exit Employees tab): its own Apps Script Web App, same idea
# as GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT_* above but bound to that other spreadsheet. See
# docs/google-apps-script-setup.md. Until set, the app falls back to the sheet's
# public share link.
EXIT_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=
EXIT_APPS_SCRIPT_SECRET=

# Finance sheet (the Real OG tab, Financials page): its own Apps Script Web App,
# same idea as EXIT_APPS_SCRIPT_* above but bound to the finance spreadsheet. See
# docs/google-apps-script-setup.md. Until set, the app falls back to the sheet's
# public share link. This sheet has payroll in it: set these, then restrict the sheet.
FINANCE_APPS_SCRIPT_URL=
FINANCE_APPS_SCRIPT_SECRET=
